## Update commands — trigger patterns and workflows

Full command reference: `project/ssot-sur/COMMANDS.md`. Recognize these patterns and execute the corresponding workflow.

| User says (pattern) | Workflow |
|---------------------|----------|
| `capture meeting: [name/link/paste/"latest"]` | Fetch notes from Notion meetings DB or paste → extract decisions, scope, answers → propose diffs to PRD-FR, open-questions.md, TDR |
| `answer: [ID] — [text]. source: [...]` | Resolve OQ row → remove `[ARCH]` if blocker clears → update FR body → update TDR story `Blocked by` → promote story to `Grooming Ready` if all blockers gone |
| `sync Notion notes` | Fetch PRD-FR + TDR Notion pages → extract inline comments/callouts → map to FRs/stories/OQs → propose updates |
| `ingest document: [file or paste]` | Read document → map content to existing FRs or propose new ones → show diff; flag conflicts |
| `update FR-[X]: [description]` | Update FR row → check TDR for affected stories → propose cascading AC/blocker updates |
| `story ready: [ID]` | Verify all `Blocked by` items resolved → set TDR status to `Grooming Ready` |
| `ADO created: [ID] = [URL]` | Fill ADO Story ID in TDR master backlog → set status to `In ADO` |
| `PRD health check` | Read-only audit: open `[ARCH]` blockers · stories blocked vs ready · FR coverage gaps · OQs without owner |
| `draft leadership update: week of [date]` | Pull status from PRD-FR + TDR + OQs → draft update → post to APC-2299 project page |
| `scope change: [description]` | Update PRD §5 scope + appendix → flag affected FRs and stories → surface related OQs |
| `push PRD` / `push TDR` / `push all` | Push pending local changes to Notion (show diff first unless user says "push directly") |

**Rule:** Every workflow follows the review-before-push sequence defined in `## Sync workflow` above. Never apply changes to Notion without showing the diff first.

## After editing any document

1. Draft locally (the `.md` file).
2. Show diff summary to user and wait for approval.
3. On approval: push to Notion using `notion-update-page`.
4. For leadership updates: post to the project page (APC-XXXX), not Brief or PRD.
5. Confirm both local and Notion are in sync before closing.
